# Screenshots are excluded with NO exception.
#
# The previous rule ignored screenshots/ but re-included
# screenshots/portfolio-picks/*.png, which is how six raw desktop captures
# reached the initial commit and stayed in a public repository until
# 2026-08-17. Two were a client tabletop-exercise deliverable, letterhead and
# all; one of those was linked from a project page as "Threat Analysis". An
# allowlisted directory becomes a place things get dropped without a second
# look, which is precisely what happened.
#
# Curated, sanitised images live in assets/screenshots/ and are added
# deliberately by path. See the screenshot rule in
# PORTFOLIO_MASTER_DOCUMENTATION.md before committing any image.
#
# Leading slash is load-bearing: a bare `screenshots/` matches the directory at
# ANY depth, so it silently swallowed assets/screenshots/ too -- caught only
# because the replacement image failed to stage.
/screenshots/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*env/
venv/

# Sensitive data
*.key
*.pem
*config.json
notification_config.json

# Certificate documents. Credential PDFs carry full name, certification
# number and issue/expiry dates -- everything needed to impersonate a
# credential holder. On 2026-08-07 four of them were dropped into
# assets/certs/ while sourcing badge art, where a `git add -A` would have
# published them permanently into the history of a public repo.
# Badge IMAGES are fine and intended; certificate DOCUMENTS are not.
*.pdf

# Agent scratch. `.claude/worktrees/` holds full checkouts of this repo, and
# `.superpowers/` holds execution ledgers and review packages. Neither belongs
# in history, and an unignored worktree directory means a `git add -A` in the
# main checkout commits an entire second copy of the tree.
.claude/
.superpowers/

# Logs
*.log

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
